Network-use source offer
------------------------
If you interact with OmniWatch over a network, you are entitled to receive the
Corresponding Source of the version you are interacting with. The source is
available at:
  https://github.com/masood1996-geo/OmniWatch
Self-hosted deployments are expected to link to their own source copy; the
dashboard footer provides a source link for this purpose.

Data attribution
----------------
OmniWatch aggregates public data. Each event carries provenance metadata
(provider, license, attribution) exposed in the API and UI. Key upstream
providers include (non-exhaustive): USGS, NASA EONET, NASA FIRMS, NOAA
(NWS/SWPC), Smithsonian GVP via GDACS (EC JRC), Safecast, adsb.lol (ODbL 1.0),
OpenSky Network, AISStream, DeepState UA, GDELT, OpenStreetMap contributors
(ODbL 1.0), PeeringDB, CelesTrak, Amtrak (retired), Fintraffic DigiTraffic,
Finnhub, Yahoo Finance (unofficial), FRED, US Treasury, BLS, UN Comtrade,
USAspending, EIA, Polymarket, OFAC, CISA, OpenSanctions, Cloudflare Radar,
IODA (Georgia Tech), WHO, ReliefWeb, Bluesky, BBC/The Guardian/Al Jazeera RSS,
SatNOGS, KiwiSDR list (linkfanel), TfL, NYC DOT, Singapore LTA.

Each provider's own license/terms govern its data. See docs/DATA_SOURCES.md
for the per-source matrix.
